    <outcome date="2026-10-02" round="r2" branch="task/uac-r2-146-r1-r2" base="task/uac-r2-146-r1 @ 8029e4456">
      <summary>Verifier round 2 (20 items; 4, 5, 12 informational) — every code item closed; open items are live gates, publish size, #1034, the PR (none may be opened here) and owner-unanswered escalations. Full per-item disposition: notes/task-146-server-child-writers.md §12 (PR description ready in §12f).</summary>
      <changes>(1) FR-E7 category routing re-owns only a communication filed under NOTHING (IsFiledOrUnreadableAsync, fail closed); NEW owner-write census in RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests — every server member that writes ownerid / ownerid@odata.bind is listed with its kind (Resolver / Seam / Routed / Root / PerUser / UnfiledOnly) and checked. (2) dataverse.update_record: a lookup change on a child table is a re-file through ReparentAsync (as-the-caller row visibility + AppendTo first; the caller's own PATCH; owner assigned and read back); another table moved under a SECURE record is refused; run-as-user classification covers POST AND PATCH. (3) External payload owner bind asserted from the real builders' payloads; builder seam guard requires the bind. (6) Owner S1 option (1) / G5 implemented for dataverse.create_record and email.draft (OwnedChildWrite): as-the-caller Create/Append privileges, AppendTo on every record named, no field-secured or owner column, then the resolver's team, then an app-only create-by-upsert; drafts record the drafter in sprk_sentby; non-child tables filed under a secure record refused. CLAUDE.md §6.5 path A recorded (note §12c). (7/8) PUT /api/v1/documents/{id} re-file asks AppendTo on each target as the caller before any owner decision (uniform 403). (9) Inbound and upload-capture emails owned from their filing are CREATED WITH that filing (IncomingAssociationResolver.BuildNewRecordFieldsAsync); unbuildable filing holds / skips. (10) Resolver looks through an un-team-owned child parent to its filing, transitively, for the secure decision and the flagged refusal (every context). (11) JobContract.IsFinalDelivery shared by the processor's dead-letter branch and the inbound hold, so the alert fires on the delivery that is dead-lettered.</changes>
