      <placement>No new service, endpoint, DI registration, option, job or package. One new internal static helper, Services/Ai/Handlers/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs (§11: existing — CallerRecordAccessProbe needs a raw bearer token the tool handlers do not hold and FinanceAuthorizationFilter is a route filter, neither runs inside a tool call; extension — reuses the probe's pure parsers ResponseGrantsPrivilege and DataverseAccessRightsMapper and the existing app-only IFieldMappingDataverseService create-by-upsert; cost of doing nothing — the two run-as-user create tools file a secure record's child in an ordinary business unit and the update tool re-files one with no owner re-derivation). New members on existing types: RecordOwnerResolution.IsSecureOwner; RecordOwnershipResolver.MaxLineageDepth / ReadUnownedChildLineageAsync; DataverseWriteItemMapper.MappedItem.Lookups / ClearedColumns + MappedLookup; IncomingAssociationResolver.BuildNewRecordFieldsAsync (extracted from the apply); JobContract.DeliveryCount / MaxDeliveryCount / IsFinalDelivery; CommunicationEnrichmentService.IsFiledOrUnreadableAsync; DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.AuthorizeRefileTargetsAsync; EmailDraftToolHandler.SenderLookupColumn; IncomingCommunicationProcessor.CreateCommunicationRecordAsync made internal. New constructor dependencies (both unconditionally registered — no asymmetric registration, §10 F.1): IRecordOwnershipResolver on the three chat tools, IFieldMappingDataverseService on the two create tools.</placement>
