    <outcome date="2026-10-02" round="b2" branch="task/uac-r2-146-b2" base="c8ede843e (task/uac-r2-146-b1 WIP 6edf97c58 + work/unified-access-control-r2 merged: origin/master 93634db58 + batch 3)">
      <summary>Every open item of the round-2 verifier closed in code and tests, except the owner question on moving a CHILD out of a secure root and the live/main-session items; owner round 7 items 3 (G5 for the AI create tools, CLAUDE.md §6.5 PATH B) and 4 (role 9 → 26 readiness) done. Full disposition: notes/task-146-server-child-writers.md §13. Merge: 17 conflicted files resolved keeping both 146's resolver owner and 152's Assigned To / acting-user contact; the event payload refusal moved into 152's BuildCreateEventPayload.</summary>
      <changes>(GAP S6a) default record thread owner tested through the FR-09 ladder with the real resolver (secure → named team, ordinary → BU team, flagged → refused/unthreaded, master keeps creator). (GAP per-member) census EveryRoutedOwnerWriteTakesItsValueFromAResolution (taint check of each Routed owner write's value) + NoServerCodeForgesAnOwnedResolution. (GAP AC10) census sees create-by-upsert (UpdateRecordFieldsAsync with a fresh / generated id), fresh-id two-argument constructions, and owner writes via Add/TryAdd and collection-initializer elements; InvoiceReviewService and SignalEvaluationService listed as Routed create sites; the per-site check requires an upsert's field map to carry the owner. (FAIL-OPEN) ReparentAsync: a failed assignment re-reads the owner — landed → stands; not landed → filing (parent lookups + AttachColumns) restored; unreadable → the safe direction (restore for a move INTO secure, keep otherwise); CRITICAL events ReparentOwnerAssignmentFailed / ReparentLeftInconsistent; "already owned" decided from the owner read AFTER the change; thread JOIN passes AttachColumns; invoice confirm deletes the invoice it created (RemoveLink cascade) when the document's owner cannot follow; G146-1 made a HARD pre-deploy gate. (LOW depth) b1's refusal at the lineage limit verified and tested. (LOW race) FR-E7 routing owner is its own If-Match write on the version read with the filing. (Round 7 item 3) dataverse.create_record: G5 for EVERY create (as-the-caller Create/Append + AppendTo on every named record + no field-secured or owner/audit column; app-only create owned by the resolver's team; the caller in the table's "for" column — sprk_todo/sprk_event sprk_assignedto, sprk_matter/sprk_project sprk_assignedtointernal, sprk_communication sprk_sentby); creator kept only for per-user tables, unfiled communications/threads (E1/E2) and non-user/team-owned tables; a root or non-ownership-set table the Secure team would own is refused (roots: task 158). email.draft unchanged in code (filed = G5, unfiled = E1). Supersession recorded: spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1 spec "Amendment A-UAC146" + its user-obo-audit note, both handlers' XML docs, OwnedChildWrite remarks, task note §13, this block. (Round 7 item 4) role JSON 26 tables; all 17 new privilege names verified against live metadata, live role read at 9 Read/Basic (read-only); guide §5.3 extension order; G146-1 commands in note §13c; new codified-set guard CodifiedSecureOwnerRoleSet_CoversEveryTableTheServerCanHandTheSecureTeam. S6 b stated as task 158 in census, note and here.</changes>
      <tests>New/extended: RecordOwnershipResolverTests +10, SecureChildOwnershipTests +5, InvoiceReviewWritePathTests +1, EmailTriageSeamTests +2 (4 reworked), SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests +9 (2 flipped), RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests +7 (21 in all); merge fixes in EventEndpointsMembershipPublishingTests, ExternalTodoScopeTests, TodoGenerationAssignedToTests, SecureChildOwnershipEndpointTests/ExternalTests/Tests, TaskActionCoreAssignedToTests, OutboundCommunicationRow. Seed-and-bite P1-P15 all bit (note §13d; P7 bit after the test was made to swap in a genuinely new row version). Counts: see the task's final report.</tests>
      <placement>No new service, endpoint, DI registration, option, job or package. Two new constructor dependencies, both unconditionally registered singletons (no asymmetric registration, §10 F.1): IFieldMappingDataverseService on CommunicationEnrichmentService (existing: the server's only If-Match write; cost of doing nothing: the routing race stays open) and IIdentityNormalizationService on DataverseCreateRecordHandler (existing: task 141's linked-contact read already used by 152's writers; cost of doing nothing: round 7's "record the person" cannot name a contact). New members on existing types only (note §13e); every owner still comes from the one resolver.</placement>
