      <summary>The b2-r1 verifier's two open findings are closed. Item 4/9: the work assignment's "for" column is now defaulted. Item 5/10: the census blind spots are closed, two by detection and the rest by KNOWN LIMITS entries. The live gates, the main-session items and the deferred tool-description follow-up stay open. Full disposition: notes/task-146-server-child-writers.md §15. PR text: §14e plus the §15e addendum.</summary>
      <changes>(Item 4/9, owner round 7 item 3 "record the person in the table's Assigned-To / 'for' column where one exists") OwnedChildWrite.ForPersonColumns now maps sprk_workassignment to sprk_assignedtointernal (contact). This is the matter/project precedent (owner A7). Task 152's AssignedToDefaults.ResponsibleContactColumns already reads that column as a work assignment's responsible internal person. The live metadata (read-only, spaarkedev1, 2026-10-02) carries it as a contact lookup. The table's separate sprk_assignedto stays model-supplied. A chat-created work assignment under an ordinary parent, or under none, is app-created, team-owned and for the caller. Under a secure parent it is still refused (task 158). One dictionary entry; owner-reversible. (Item 5/10, census) New OwnerKeyLiteral: $"ownerid", @"ownerid", $@"…" and @$"…" (with no holes) are owner keys in the owner-write census, the value check, the per-site check and OwnerKeyConst. HardCodedId also refuses Guid.TryParse and ParseExact. New HandedToACreate: a row given a caller-chosen id counts as a create when the same member hands it to Create(…), Create…Async(…) or new CreateRequest { Target = … }. This applies to the two-argument, initializer and LogicalName-assignment forms, and FreshEntityCreate now accepts a member-access id. Added to KNOWN LIMITS: an upsert of a caller-chosen id; a create in another member or file; a target-typed new("t"); a key interpolated with holes; a conditional or coalesce owner value whose other branch is not a resolution; a reassigned tainted name. Grep: no prefixed owner key in src/server, and the real tree's counts are unchanged. (Item 6) The model-facing tool description is deferred to the main session, unchanged (note §13b). (Item 15) S6 b stays task 158 (owner round 6).</changes>
