    <outcome date="2026-10-03" round="c1" branch="task/uac-r2-146-c1" base="task/uac-r2-146-b2-r2 @ 390e9ff29 + work/unified-access-control-r2 @ 6b243f092 merged (8f3f30f44, clean; owner rounds 10-11) + main-session WIP snapshot 6cd0c3f28">
      <summary>Owner rounds 10 and 11 applied. (1) Round 10 item 7, BINDING: moving a CHILD out of a secure root is an un-secure, so F3 applies. IRecordOwnershipResolver.ReparentAsync, which every BFF re-file goes through, asks F3 BEFORE any write: Full Access (Write + Delete, RetrievePrincipalAccess as the caller) on EVERY secure root the child leaves (to no secure root or to a different one), or the child's own creator (sprk_createdbyperson read by its logical name, else createdby). Refused otherwise with task 150's reason codes (sdap.unsecure.not_permitted / sdap.unsecure.permission_unverifiable) and the unsecure endpoint's 403 ProblemDetails shape. The ONE F3 helper is Services/Access/SecureDesignationRemoval.cs; the second draft is deleted. UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs is NOT touched: the F3 check exists only on task/uac-r2-150 (a89f3c8cd), and note §16c gives the exact replacement that makes 150's private method call the helper at integration, with the four behaviour differences. (2) Round 10 item 8: E1 ACCEPTED, no behaviour change; MessagingIngestor's census waiver Pending to Permanent; code comments cite the decision. (3) Every open escalation re-checked against rounds 10-11 (note §16d): child move-out, E1, trigger 3 (round 11 item 4: intersection, task 149), E3/G146-2 (round 11 approved) are closed; E2 stays with task 149. Full disposition: notes/task-146-server-child-writers.md §16.</summary>
      <changes>RecordOwnershipResolver: RecordReparent.SecureExitCaller; RecordOwnerResolution.SecureRemovalRefusal / IsForbidden / SecureRemovalRefused; ReparentAsync gate (RefuseUnlessPermittedToLeaveSecureRootsAsync, SecureRootsAboveAsync: secure roots above the parents before minus after, through child parents up to MaxLineageDepth; a row held in the Secure BU whose root cannot be named admits only its creator); KeepCreator doc cites round 10 item 8. SecureDesignationRemoval (the kept draft): Full Access asked before the creator-person read; an absent creator column is unverifiable, never allowed. ProblemDetailsHelper.RecordOwnerRefused: a forbidden refusal is SecureRemovalDecision.ToProblem (403 / 500, title, detail, reasonCode, traceId). Callers: PUT /api/v1/documents/{id}, associate-record and PUT /api/v1/events/{id} pass SecureRemovalCaller.ForRequest(CallerRecordAccessProbe, HttpContext) and the trace id; dataverse.update_record passes its user client (WhoAmI + OwnedChildWrite.RightsOnAsync, extracted from the AppendTo check) and reports a forbidden refusal with its code. Person-less writers (DataverseUpdateHandler, UpdateRecordActionCore, IncomingAssociationResolver, the thread JOIN, InvoiceReviewService) pass none, so a move out is refused (unverifiable). MessagingIngestor: comment at the create. Census: MessagingIngestor waiver Permanent.</changes>
      <tests>New: tests/unit/domain/Auth/SecureDesignationRemovalTests.cs (10: Full Access permitted; creator permitted with no probe; recorded creator person permitted; Write-only refused not_permitted 403; probe throws unverifiable 500; caller unknown or absent unverifiable 403 (x2); creator column absent unverifiable; two roots need Full Access on each; the refusal renders 150's ProblemDetails). RecordOwnershipResolverTests +8 (the gate: Full Access on the root left; creator; recorded person; Write-only refused before any write; person-less writer refused; secure to secure asks the root left; staying under the root asks nothing; a child of a secure message asks the root above). End to end over the real resolver: SecureChildOwnershipDocumentRefileTests +3, SecureChildOwnershipEndpointTests +4, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests +2. Changed with the contract: 4 resolver move-out tests pass a Full Access caller; 2 event re-file tests grant Full Access on the secure project; 2 DataverseUpdateHandler move-out tests now assert the refusal; the hosts register an F3 probe double. Seed-and-bite S1-S8 (note §16f), run on the final source. Counts, each suite run once in full: BFF unit 14,389 passed / 14 failed / 54 skipped (14,457); the 14 were HTTP-client timeouts after about 3 minutes under machine-wide contention (5 or more concurrent testhosts), and their 13 classes re-run in isolation passed 135 / 135. ArchTests 372 / 372; Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests 104 / 104; Spe.Integration.Tests 403 passed / 0 failed / 25 skipped. Affected first: 416 / 416, census and route guards 41 / 41.</tests>
      <placement>No new service, endpoint, DI registration, option, job, column or package. One new static helper with its question/answer types, Services/Access/SecureDesignationRemoval.cs (CLAUDE.md §11: existing = task 150's F3 check, a private method on an unmerged branch, and nothing on this branch; extension = the same rule lifted out and generalized (the root whose Full Access counts and the record whose creator counts can differ) so the unsecure endpoint and the re-file path share ONE check; cost of doing nothing = any Write and AppendTo holder can move a secure root's child into an ordinary business unit, un-securing it without the rights owner round 10 item 7 requires). New handler parameters: CallerRecordAccessProbe ([FromServices]) on three re-file routes, registered unconditionally (no asymmetric registration, §10 F.1). ADR-002: no plugin. ADR-003: an unknown caller, an unread root, a read fault, an absent column or a person-less writer refuses before any write. Publish size: main session.</placement>
      <ship-together>Owner round 11 item 3: 146 and 149 may deploy (together); no record is unsecured in a shared environment until task 148 is deployed. Task 152 ordering unchanged (owner B2).</ship-together>
      <manual-gates>Unchanged and approved by owner round 11 (dev, dry run then apply then verify): G146-1 (a HARD pre-deploy gate), G146-2, G146-4 (probes on TEST records; the main session creates the non-admin test user). G146-3 and G146-5 are not named in round 11; the main session confirms that "all of them" covers them. Integration steps for the main session: note §16c (150's private method calls SecureDesignationRemoval; the resolver's sprk_createdbyperson constant becomes task 133's RecordCreatorPerson.Column; task 133's stamp in the G5 create payload).</manual-gates>
      <not-closed>The F3 integration with task 150 (main session, note §16c). E2 (Direct and master threads) stays with task 149. AC11, AC13, AC14, AC16 as before (main session). Owner option, not a blocker: fold the update tool's re-file step into path B.</not-closed>
