      <summary>The c1 verifier's items and owner round 13 (items 3, 6, 7, 8, 9) are applied. (1) The re-file gate's fail-closed rules are now pinned by tests and seeds: a Secure-BU row whose secure root cannot be named admits only its creator; a filing deeper than the lineage limit refuses; the gate's own ambiguous-Secure-BU refusal is reachable (through a KeepCreator row) and tested; the update tool words an F3 refusal as an authorization answer. (2) Round 13 item 8: a playbook update that impersonates a user is asked F3 AS THAT USER (RetrievePrincipalAccess with MSCRMCallerID); only truly person-less writers are refused. (3) Round 13 item 9: children the BFF creates as the application record the person who asked in sprk_createdbyperson (17 child tables, a new schema script, never applied here), stamped by every app-create writer that acts for a person through the one resolver; F3's creator branch reads it for children. A table without the column answers "unverifiable". (4) Round 13 item 7: the update tool's re-file is folded into path B (spec Amendment A-UAC146); no .claude ADR text is needed. (5) Write-path I-2 and I-6 are current. (6) Round 13 items 3 and 6 are recorded. Full disposition: notes/task-146-server-child-writers.md §17. PR text: §14e + §15e + §16h + §17l.</summary>
      <changes>(Items 1-3) Tests only for the gate: RecordOwnershipResolverTests (unidentified secure root by a Full Access non-creator and by its creator; the depth limit; the ambiguous Secure BU before F3) and SecureDesignationRemovalTests (an unidentified secure record with no named root is never permitted for a non-creator, even with Full Access; its creator is). The secureBu.Ambiguous branch is KEPT: it is reached by a cleared communication that keeps its creator (E1), whose owner decision reads no business unit. (Item 4) The Write-only update-tool test pins the F3 refusal's message prefix and the absence of the owner-refusal wording. (Item 5) DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md: I-6 E1 accepted (round 10 item 8); I-2 adds the c1 F3 gate, the c1-r1 impersonation and creator-person rules, path B for the update tool's re-file, G146-1 applied in dev. (Items 6 and 20) UpdateRecordActionCore passes SecureRemovalCaller.ForImpersonatedUser(person, IDataverseRecordShareService) when it impersonates; new IDataverseRecordShareService.GetPrincipalRightsAsync (a faulting default body) over the new DataverseWebApiService.RetrievePrincipalRightsAsync (MSCRMCallerID via DataverseImpersonation; 403/404 = no rights, any other failure throws = unverifiable). (Items 7 and 21) RecordOwnershipContext.RequestedBy (RecordRequester: systemuserid or Entra object id, server-derived); the resolver resolves it after the owner decision into RecordOwnerResolution.CreatedByPerson (object id looked up, TOP 2, exactly one user; unknown records nobody and refuses nothing; a refused owner never reads it); ApplyTo and StampCreatorOn stamp it only on a table that carries the column. ReparentAsync reads the creator person for children (an absent column, fault 0x80041103 measured read-only, answers unverifiable). RecordCreatorPerson (task 133's file plus StampedChildTables (17), NavigationProperty, Bind, IsStamped widened) and Spaarke.Dataverse.RecordCreatorPersonColumn (the spelling shared by the seams). Writers that act for a person now stamp it: OwnedChildWrite (G5 creates; a caller-supplied sprk_createdbyperson is refused), POST documents, events and their log rows (Delete/Complete/Cancel gained an HttpContext parameter), analysis create/fork/promote, AnalysisResultPersistence (profile outputs, review memo), the Compose promoter, the file-version create, CommunicationService (sends, archive rows, on-demand archive), EmailUploadCaptureService, MessageAttachmentMaterializer, ThreadResolver's record thread, the Job B apply audit rows and created task (TaskActionCore/ActionSeam RequestedBySystemUserId), the Office save (carried on the job payload to UploadFinalizationWorker), the Office quick-create invoice and To Do, and the G5 invoice confirm (InvoiceReviewConfirmRequest.RequestedBy, JsonIgnore). The seams take the person as they take the team (CreatedByPersonId on CreateDocumentRequest, AnalysisOutputEntity, CreateEventRequest; optional createdByPersonId on CreateAnalysisAsync and CreateEventLogAsync). New scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 (dry run / -Apply / -Verify; the same profiles as task 133; solution membership checked by table inclusion); dry run run read-only against spaarkedev1, -Apply NOT run. Census: every census child table carries the column and stays inside the codified set; 48 person-bearing writer members must name their person; 13 person-less writers listed with reasons. (Item 8) A child under two secure roots that leaves one asks F3 on the root it leaves (the stricter reading, from round 11's intersection rule); recorded for the owner. (Items 17, 18) G146-3/5 covered by round 11; 150's F3 method calls the shared helper at integration, its four behaviour differences accepted. (Item 19) Path B: spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1 spec.md (MUST marker, Amendment A-UAC146) and notes/user-obo-audit.md, DataverseUpdateRecordHandler XML doc, OwnedChildWrite remarks, write-path I-2, note §12c and §14c marked superseded, amendment R13 below.</changes>
      <tests>New test cases (a Theory counts once per InlineData): RecordOwnershipResolverTests +12, SecureDesignationRemovalTests +2, SecureChildOwnershipTests +5, SecureChildOwnershipWriterTests +3, SecureChildOwnershipEndpointTests +1, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests +1, EventEndpointsMembershipPublishingTests +2, InvoiceReviewWritePathTests +3, the new ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchemaAgreementTests (7) and RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests +3. Existing tests now assert the stamp: the G5 secure create, the record thread, the apply audit row, the Compose promote, and the Office save, To Do and invoice. The Write-only update-tool test pins the F3 message prefix. Contract-change fixes: the CreateAnalysisAsync and CreateEventLogAsync mocks, two ResolveOwnerAsync stubs, RecordingEventService, RecordOwnershipResolverDouble, OwnershipDirectory.WithoutColumn, and the Office test auth handler's optional X-Test-Oid. Seed-and-bite: A, K, L, B, J, G, P1b, P2 and C1-C9 all bit (P1 was void: it did not compile, so P1b replaced it). Each plant was restored byte-identical and touched (note §17g). Each suite was run once in full: BFF unit 14,427 passed / 12 failed / 54 skipped (14,493). The 12 failures were HttpClient timeouts under machine-wide contention (7 testhosts, 268 dotnet processes); their 12 classes re-run in isolation passed 172 / 172. ArchTests 375 / 375; Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests 104 / 104; Spe.Integration.Tests 403 passed / 0 failed / 25 skipped. No vulnerable package, and no package change. ADR-038: no banned shapes.</tests>
      <placement>No new service, endpoint, DI registration, option, job or package. NEW COLUMN sprk_createdbyperson on 17 child tables (with a relationship each), created by a NEW script scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 (CLAUDE.md §11: existing = task 133's same column on the three roots and its script, createdby, createdonbehalfby, the "for" columns; extension = the same column, profiles and helper extended to the children, in a second script because 133's script and its agreement test are on an unmerged branch and pin the root set; createdby is the application user for an app-only create and the "for" columns name who a record is FOR, not who asked; cost of doing nothing = F3's creator branch can never admit the person who made a BFF-created child, so only Full Access holders could move a G5 create, an Office save, an outbound email or an invoice out of a secure record, which owner round 13 item 9 rejects). NEW SEAM MEMBER IDataverseRecordShareService.GetPrincipalRightsAsync with DataverseWebApiService.RetrievePrincipalRightsAsync and SecureRemovalCaller.ForImpersonatedUser (§11: existing = CallerRecordAccessProbe needs a bearer token a playbook does not hold, OwnedChildWrite.RightsOnAsync needs the chat tool's OBO client, the share seam reads POA shares not effective rights; extension = one member on the existing record-access seam, impersonating through the existing DataverseImpersonation helper the impersonated PATCH already uses, with a faulting default body so the existing doubles stay fail closed; cost of doing nothing = owner round 13 item 8 unmet: a confirming user's Job B update moving a child out of a secure root is refused even when that user holds Full Access). New members and parameters on existing types only (note §17h); one new static file, Spaarke.Dataverse/RecordCreatorPersonColumn.cs, spells the column once for the seams and the BFF. ADR-002: no plugin. ADR-003: an absent column, a rights fault and a missing seam all answer unverifiable; an unknown requester records nobody. ADR-010: no new DI registration. Publish size: not measured here (task brief).</placement>
      <manual-gates>NEW G146-6, a HARD pre-deploy gate (owner round 13 item 9 approved the schema step as a dev live step): a BFF carrying c1-r1 writes sprk_createdbyperson on the child tables, and Dataverse refuses a create that names a missing column. Before deploying this code, from a short path inside PowerShell: scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 -EnvironmentUrl https://spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com -BffApplicationIds 5967251e-171c-46fe-a6c2-ef843c90309d,1e40baad-e065-4aea-a8d4-4b7ab273458c (dry run), then the same with -Apply, then with -Verify (exit 0), then a read-only GET {entityset}?$select=_sprk_createdbyperson_value&amp;$top=1 per table (note §17i). G146-4 also confirms that one app-created child per family records the probe user, and that the probe user can move their own app-created child out of a secure root while a second Collaborate user cannot. G146-3 and G146-5 are covered by owner round 11's "all of them" (round 13 item 3). G146-1 (applied in dev) and G146-2 (done): unchanged.</manual-gates>
      <not-closed>AC13: publish size and #1034 (main session). AC16: no PR from this session; text in note §14e + §15e + §16h + §17l. AC11: G146-4 (live, after the deploy with 149). AC14 / round 13 item 9: G146-6 (live, pre-deploy, main session) and the 17 evidence entries copied in at integration. Integration (main session): task 150's F3 method calls SecureDesignationRemoval (§16c, owner-accepted); task 133's RecordCreatorPerson.cs add/add conflict (take this branch's file, re-apply any later 133 change) and its interim DataverseCreateRecordHandler stamp removed, keeping the IsNamedIn refusals (§17e). E2 stays with task 149. The tool-description follow-up (§13b) stays with the main session.</not-closed>
