  <amendments>
    <amendment n="R3" date="2026-09-30" source="owner round 3 (session27 note) — BINDING">(S5 REVERSED) Never create a record nobody can see: inbound email (or any server create) whose secure parent cannot be determined is NOT created owned by the memberless secure team. Retry transient failures; if still undeterminable, leave it unprocessed in the ingestion queue (dead-letter/hold) and alert administrators (appnotification to an admin principal) with enough detail to resolve it; nothing is written to Dataverse until resolved. Escalation trigger S5 is resolved this way.</amendment>
  </amendments>
  <amendments>
    <amendment n="R10-R11" date="2026-10-03" source="owner rounds 10 and 11 (session27 note) — BINDING">Escalations closed by the owner. (a) Round 10 item 7: moving a CHILD out of a secure root is an un-secure, so F3 applies (Full Access holders plus the creator); implemented in c1. (b) Round 10 item 8: E1 ACCEPTED, unfiled communications keep their creator and filed ones are routed secure-if-any; MessagingIngestor's waiver is Permanent. (c) Round 11 item 4 answers trigger 3: a child under two secure roots gets the INTERSECTION of their sharee sets, ShareAccess is not mirrored onto children (task 149 implements it). (d) Round 11 approves G146-2 (Read on sprk_emailreviewlog for the BU default teams), closing E3 as an escalation; G146-1 (role 9 to 26), probes on TEST records and the BFF deploy are approved too. (e) Round 11 item 3 refines the ship-together constraint: 146 and 149 may deploy, but no record is unsecured in a shared environment until task 148 is deployed. Still open: E2 (Direct and master threads), with task 149. Escalation triggers 2 (record threads, answered by owner S6), 5 (run-as-user writers, answered by owner S1 / G5 and round 7 item 3) and 6 (task 152 ordering, owner B2) were already closed.</amendment>
  </amendments>
  <amendments>
    <amendment n="R13" date="2026-10-03" source="owner round 13 (session27 note) — BINDING">Answers to the c1 verifier's questions. (a) Item 3: G146-3 and G146-5 are covered by round 11's "all of them". (b) Item 6: the shared F3 helper's behaviour is kept and supersedes task 150's private check at integration (the four differences in note §16c are accepted). (c) Item 7: the update tool's app-only re-file step is folded into ADR path B (spec Amendment A-UAC146), as round 8 did for 156's re-stamp; the path-A record is superseded. (d) Item 8: a playbook writer that impersonates a user is checked under F3 AS THAT USER; only truly person-less writers are refused. (e) Item 9: sprk_createdbyperson is added to the governed child tables, stamped by every app-create writer through the RecordCreatorPerson helper, and read by F3's creator branch for children; the schema step is a dev live step (G146-6). Implemented in c1-r1 (note §17).</amendment>
  </amendments>
  <amendments>
    <amendment n="Q12" date="2026-10-01" source="owner — BINDING">Scope confirmation (from the task 130 verifier, 2026-10-01): sprk_invoice IS a child of a secure matter or project. Its ownership is already resolved team-first by task 130 (RecordOwnershipResolver, record-first from the matter), but 146 must include sprk_invoice in its writer census and in the codified child-table set (145/082 JSON) so invoices filed to secure records are covered by every path, including Office quick-create (OfficeService) and InvoiceReviewService.</amendment>
  </amendments>
</task>
